    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Thyroid nodules in McCune&ndash;Albright syndrome",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "The thyroid nodules exhibit papillary architecture with the formation of true papillae that have fibrovascular cores, but the papillae are organized in a centripetal fashion within the follicles and they are lined by uniform epithelial cells with bland, basally located nuclei.",
    "source": "",
    "copyright": "Asa&nbsp;SL",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/67/36/27841.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/67/36/thumb_27841.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 80950,
    "bookid": 67,
    "chapterId": 36,
    "fileId": 39083,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Thyroid nodules in McCune&ndash;Albright syndrome",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Despite the formation of true papillae, the follicular epithelial cells forming the thyroid nodules have uniform, bland cytology with round, basal nuclei that have dark chromatin.",
    "source": "",
    "copyright": "Asa&nbsp;SL",
    "tablehtml": "",
